{#-
  House state summary prompt.

  Produces a compact description of current house state for an LLM to summarise.

  REPLACE BEFORE USE:
    <indoor_temp>  — an indoor temperature sensor
    <outdoor_temp> — an outdoor temperature sensor
    <house_power>  — whole-house power draw, in watts

  Everything else iterates over domains and device classes rather than naming
  entities, so it works unmodified on any install.

  Keep the output constraint in the prompt AND truncate the response — input_text
  helpers are capped at 255 characters and will fail silently past that.

  Keep the output constraint in the prompt AND truncate the response — input_text
  helpers are capped at 255 characters and will fail silently past that.
-#}

You are summarising the current state of a home. Write ONE sentence, under 200
characters, in plain British English. Mention only what is notable or unusual —
skip anything that is in its normal state. No preamble, no lists, no emoji.

Current state:

People:
{% for person in states.person -%}
  - {{ person.name }}: {{ person.state }}
{% endfor %}

Occupancy:
{% for sensor in states.binary_sensor
   if sensor.attributes.device_class in ['occupancy', 'motion', 'presence']
   and sensor.state == 'on' -%}
  - {{ sensor.name }}: detected
{% endfor %}

Lights on:
{% set lights_on = states.light | selectattr('state', 'eq', 'on') | list %}
{% if lights_on | count == 0 -%}
  - none
{% else -%}
{% for light in lights_on -%}
  - {{ light.name }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

Media:
{% set playing = states.media_player | selectattr('state', 'eq', 'playing') | list %}
{% if playing | count == 0 -%}
  - nothing playing
{% else -%}
{% for mp in playing -%}
  - {{ mp.name }}: {{ mp.attributes.media_title | default('playing', true) }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

Climate:
  - Indoor: {{ states('sensor.<indoor_temp>') }}°C
  - Outdoor: {{ states('sensor.<outdoor_temp>') }}°C

Power:
  - Current draw: {{ states('sensor.<house_power>') }} W

Doors and windows open:
{% set open = states.binary_sensor
   | selectattr('attributes.device_class', 'in', ['door', 'window', 'garage_door'])
   | selectattr('state', 'eq', 'on') | list %}
{% if open | count == 0 -%}
  - all closed
{% else -%}
{% for s in open -%}
  - {{ s.name }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
